R-IN8 R-IN2 R-IN7 R-SM2 R-C10 R-TG1 (slice 055, answer Q4 of the review): `tln init --platform acme/mov`. The platform has 2 releases. 0.2.0 (the start release: the highest version) has a `requires` clause with an alias and a record (`[Model : model] for program : { init!, update! }`). 0.1.0 has `requires {} { main! : () => {} }`. The directory has a `talon.toml` with `[build] target = "wasm32"`, and 0.2.0 has the target x64musl only: R-C10 makes it no candidate, so the resolve moves the platform to 0.1.0 (wasm32, x64musl). `init` then makes the stub again from the header of 0.1.0 and writes `main.roc` again with the `pf` URL of 0.1.0 and the pin: `main! = || crash "write the app"`, with no `Model` and no `program` (a stub of 0.2.0 would not build for 0.1.0). `init` made the file, so this is no overwrite of a file of a user (R-IN7).
